        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: வளைவு",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "வளைவு — vaḷaivu — \"a curve; a bend\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "இந்த மலைச் சாலையில் நிறைய வளைவுகள் இருக்கின்றன. inta malaic cālaiyil niṟaiya vaḷaivukaḷ irukkiṉṟaṉa. There are many bends on this hill road."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: வளைவுகள், vaḷaivukaḷ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "From வளை, to bend, + the noun ending -வு."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "வளைவு (vaḷaivu) is built from வளை, \"to bend, to become crooked\" (DEDR 5314), with the noun ending -vu."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
